{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.ClosureNormalisationDefect","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.spuriousBinding_absorbed_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.spuriousBinding_absorbed_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SpuriousClosureBinding.lean#L147-L163","doc":"**With the level factor restored, the spurious binding is exactly zero.** The same\nnon-interacting assembly that registered `m · log δ` in `spuriousBinding_eq` registers nothing once\nthe `δ^{level}` normalisation is applied. So the artefact is a defect of the *unnormalised*\nconvention, not of the physics — and the fix is the normalisation the framework already uses for the\nwrithe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.freeEnergy_absorb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.freeEnergy_absorb","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SpuriousClosureBinding.lean#L142-L145","doc":"The free energy of the absorbed amplitude is that of the bare trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.closureNorm_absorb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.closureNorm_absorb","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SpuriousClosureBinding.lean#L135-L140","doc":"**Absorbing the closure normalisation.** Multiplying by `δ^{level}` — the `d^{level}` slot of\n`MarkovMoves.normFactor` with `d = δ` — recovers the unnormalised trace exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.spuriousPerNucleon_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.spuriousPerNucleon_mono","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SpuriousClosureBinding.lean#L109-L120","doc":"**It does not vanish in the large-assembly limit — it saturates.** The per-component artefact is\nmonotone increasing in the component count, so it approaches the constant `log δ` from below rather\nthan washing out. A constant per-nucleon offset is exactly the shape of a plateau, which is why this\nis worth stating rather than dismissing as small. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.spuriousPerNucleon_lt_log","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.spuriousPerNucleon_lt_log","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SpuriousClosureBinding.lean#L100-L107","doc":"**Per component the artefact is bounded by `log δ` and never reaches it.** For an `m+1`-component\nassembly the spurious binding per component is `m·log δ/(m+1) < log δ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.physicalBinding_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.physicalBinding_eq","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SpuriousClosureBinding.lean#L92-L98","doc":"**The correction.** The physical binding is the naively-computed one minus the closure artefact.\nStated as the identity a consumer needs: whatever `B_naive` a trace-route computation reports for an\nassembly with interaction free energy `B_phys`, the two differ by exactly `m · log δ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.spuriousBinding_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.spuriousBinding_pos","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SpuriousClosureBinding.lean#L83-L90","doc":"**The artefact always has the sign of binding.** For `δ > 1` and at least one joining, the\nspurious term is strictly positive — it can never present as anti-binding, so a sign check cannot\ndetect it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.loopValue_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.loopValue_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SpuriousClosureBinding.lean#L75-L81","doc":"**The substrate loop value exceeds one.** For `q > 1`, `δ = q + q⁻¹ > 1`. `loopValue_ne_one`\ngives only `≠ 1`; the strict inequality is what pins the SIGN of the artefact below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.spuriousBinding_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SpuriousClosureBinding.spuriousBinding_eq","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SpuriousClosureBinding.lean#L64-L73","doc":"**A non-interacting assembly registers binding `m · log δ`.** The left-hand side is the\nmass-deficit binding — sum over isolated components minus the assembled value — for an assembly whose\n*only* difference from its parts is the closure normalisation. It is not zero. ","signatureChunk":0}]}